<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/110d895ec19f> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[271] 2 autonomous vehicles, one powered by Google and the other from Delphi Automotive, nearly collided this week in what’s thought to be the first close call between a pair of self-driving cars, Reuters reports." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "271" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/1d725d5f5897> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[272] It has been reported that a Delphi Automotive-owned self driving Audi was forced to take ‘appropriate action’ in order to avoid crashing into a Google self driving Lexus after it was cut off by the car." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "272" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8ae9fc3fb7ec> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Since September, any accident must be reported to the state Department of Motor Vehicles. The agency said there have been four, but would not comment about fault or anything else, citing California law that collision reports are confidential." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "275" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f0ba634f4c16> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[271] 2 autonomous vehicles, one powered by Google and the other from Delphi Automotive, nearly collided this week in what’s thought to be the first close call between a pair of self-driving cars, Reuters reports." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "271" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/00964a1710d0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The California Department of Motor Vehicles has also backed up the stories by both companies, saying that neither was at fault during the incident." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "272" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/099cc496836d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Delphi’s John Absmeier told Reuters." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "271" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/11bb1e510888> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Chris Urmson, director of the program, said that none of the self driving cars were the cause of any incidents and many of the incidents were caused by other cars driving into the back of the Google vehicles." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "272" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/242429e500c5> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The national rate for reported \"property-damage-only crashes\" is about 0.3 per 100,000 miles driven, according to data from the National Highway Traffic Safety Administration." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "275" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3e05c78a9b1e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "John Simpson, a longtime critic of Google as privacy project director of the nonprofit Consumer Watchdog, pointed out that the company's ultimate goal is a car without a steering wheel or pedals." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "275" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/429cb9a3ca98> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "John Absmeier was traveling in the Delphi Audi Q5 self driving car on San Antonio Road in Palo Alto, California when the clash happened." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "272" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7f0108be61dc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Absmeier told Reuters that his vehicle was negotiating a lane change when the Google vehicle cut it off, causing the Audi to take “appropriate action” to avoid a crash." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "273" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ca12974c7fd6> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "After the incident, it was reported by Reuters as a ‘close call’ who used Absmeier’s comments in their article." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "272" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/dc17f08662cb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Kristin Kinley, a Delphi spokeswoman, has said “The story was taken completely out of context when describing a type of complex driving scenario that can occur in the real world." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "272" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e418933f68e9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A Delphi spokesperson emailed Fortune with the following statement." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "271" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f5311a5862a8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "It has been reported that a Delphi Automotive-owned self driving Audi was forced to take ‘appropriate action’ in order to avoid crashing into a Google self driving Lexus after it was cut off by the car." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "272" .

